{"alignments": [{"id": "JON.3.1.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.1.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.1.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JON.3.1.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.1.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.1.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JON.3.1.a003", "note": "The supplied definite article belongs to the anarthrous nominal expression.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.1.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.1.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JON.3.1.a004", "note": "The nomen rectum takes “of” under the construct-chain rule.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.1.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.1.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004", "t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JON.3.1.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.1.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.1.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JON.3.1.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.1.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.1.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JON.3.1.a007", "note": "The substantive adverb is expanded as “the second time,” headed on its lexical anchor “second.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.1.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.1.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JON.3.1.a008", "note": "The preposition of לֵאמֹר has no separate English realization.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.1.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.1.008", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.1.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.1.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.1.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}], "ref": "JON.3.1", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JON.3.2.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a005", "note": "The ASV demonstrative “that” occupies the determiner position and realizes this article.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a007", "note": "The ASV writes only one determiner for the definite noun and its agreeing adjective; the first article takes it.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.007", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a010", "note": "The ASV chose “preach”; its margin offers the competing rendering “cry.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a013", "note": "The definite object marker is not separately rendered.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.013", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a014", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.014"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.015"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a016", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.016"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a017", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.017"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a018", "note": "The participle is finitely recast as “bid.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.018"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a019", "note": "The ASV promotes the prepositional object to a bare English object.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.019"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.019", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.2.a020", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.2.020"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.2.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}], "ref": "JON.3.2", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JON.3.3.a001", "note": "The waw is rendered by “So.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a008", "note": "The preposition כְּ is rendered by the compound English preposition “according to,” headed on its lexical anchor “according”; the following construct noun takes only “the word.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a009", "note": "The anarthrous construct noun licenses the supplied definite article and takes “the word”; “to” belongs to the preceding compound preposition.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a010", "note": "As the nomen rectum, the divine name takes “of Jehovah.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a011", "note": "The waw is rendered by “Now.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a013", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a014", "note": "The noun licenses the discontinuous English expression “an … city.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.014"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017", "t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.015"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a016", "note": "Hebrew “unto God” is an indivisible intensifying expression rendered as “exceeding”; with no uniquely defensible internal source head, the first source token is the deterministic display anchor.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.016", "WLC.JON.3.3.017"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.016", "status": "noncompositional", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a017", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.018"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024"], "target_head": "t024"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a018", "note": "The dependent construct numeral takes “of three.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.019"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021", "t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "JON.3.3.a019", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.3.020"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.3.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}], "ref": "JON.3.3", "review_notes": ["The ASV margin gives the underlying Hebrew expression as “a city great unto God”; the alignment follows the main-text intensifier “exceeding.”"], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JON.3.4.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a002", "note": "The explicit subject Jonah is aligned separately.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a004", "note": "The purpose preposition takes the English infinitive marker.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a007", "note": "The assimilated article is a real morpheme and takes “the.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a010", "note": "The indefinite article belongs to the noun licensing “a day’s.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a011", "note": "The numeral “one” is not separately expressed beyond the English singular indefinite phrase.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.011", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a013", "note": "The subject pronoun realizes the verb's person and number.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013", "t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a014", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.014"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.015"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a016", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.016"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a017", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.017"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a018", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.018"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a019", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.019"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a020", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.020"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "JON.3.4.a021", "note": "The participial predicate is rendered by the passive future phrase, headed on “overthrown.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.4.021"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.4.021", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022", "t023", "t024"], "target_head": "t024"}], "ref": "JON.3.4"