{"alignments": [{"id": "JON.3.5.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a002", "note": "The explicit subject “the people of Nineveh” is aligned separately.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a003", "note": "The construct noun licenses the supplied definite article.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a004", "note": "The nomen rectum takes “of.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004", "t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a005", "note": "The ASV recasts belief in God with a bare direct object.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.005", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a008", "note": "The subject pronoun realizes the verb's person and number.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a009", "note": "The noun licenses the English indefinite article.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a011", "note": "The verb is rendered by the phrasal verb “put on,” headed on “put.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014", "t015"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a013", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a014", "note": "The anarthrous substantive takes the supplied “the” and is rendered by the superlative “greatest.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.014"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018", "t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a015", "note": "The suffix is rendered by the English genitival pronoun phrase “of them.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.015"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020", "t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a016", "note": "The waw is rendered by the connective “even.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.016"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a017", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.017"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a018", "note": "The anarthrous substantive takes the supplied “the” and is rendered by the superlative “least.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.018"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024", "t025"], "target_head": "t025"}, {"id": "JON.3.5.a019", "note": "The suffix is rendered by the English genitival pronoun phrase “of them.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.5.019"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.5.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t026", "t027"], "target_head": "t027"}], "ref": "JON