{"alignments": [{"id": "JON.3.6.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a004", "note": "The ASV renders the Hebrew word as “tidings”; the margin preserves the competing literal rendering “word.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a005", "note": "The ASV's transitive “reached” leaves the goal preposition without a separate word.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.005", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a006", "note": "The anarthrous construct noun licenses the supplied “the.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a007", "note": "The nomen rectum takes “of.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a009", "note": "The subject pronoun realizes the verb's person and number.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a013", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a014", "note": "The ASV lexically renders the removal verb as “laid.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.014"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.015"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a016", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.016"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a017", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.017"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a018", "note": "The compound Hebrew relation is reduced to “from,” already carried by the preceding preposition.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.018"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.018", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a019", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.019"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a020", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.020"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a021", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.021"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.021", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a022", "note": "The English object “him” has no source object morpheme; it is not absorbed into the verb's rendering.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a023", "note": "The noun's adverbial function licenses “with.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.022"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.022", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024", "t025"], "target_head": "t025"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a024", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.023"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.023", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t026"], "target_head": "t026"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a025", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.024"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.024", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t027"], "target_head": "t027"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a026", "note": "The ASV renders the preposition by “in.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.025"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.025", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t028"], "target_head": "t028"}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a027", "note": "The ASV writes no definite article before “ashes.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.026"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.026", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.6.a028", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.6.027"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.6.027", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t029"], "target_head": "t029"}], "ref": "JON.3.6", "review_notes": ["The ASV margin gives the competing clause-level rendering “For word came unto the king”; the alignment follows the main text."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JON.3.7.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a002", "note": "The verb's light-verb rendering “made proclamation” heads on the lexical complement “proclamation”; its person licenses “he.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a004", "note": "The ASV main text renders Hebrew “said” contextually as “published”; the margin preserves the literal alternative.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a007", "note": "The source preposition is rendered contextually by “by.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a008", "note": "The anarthrous construct noun licenses the supplied “the.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a010", "note": "As nomen rectum it carries “of”; the unit is discontinuous around its article.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a012", "note": "The substantival adjective is rendered lexically as “nobles.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a013", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a014", "note": "The preposition of לֵאמֹר has no English realization.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.014"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.014", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.015"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a016", "note": "The ASV writes no article before “man.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.016"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.016", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a017", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.017"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a018", "note": "The waw is rendered by “nor.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.018"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a019", "note": "The ASV writes no article before “beast.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.019"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.019", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a020", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.020"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023"], "target_head": "t023"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a021", "note": "The ASV writes no article before “herd.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.021"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.021", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a022", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.022"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.022", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t024"], "target_head": "t024"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a023", "note": "The waw is rendered by “nor.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.023"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.023", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t025"], "target_head": "t025"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a024", "note": "The ASV writes no article before “flock.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.024"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.024", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a025", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.025"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.025", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t026"], "target_head": "t026"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a026", "note": "The clause-initial negative is rendered by “neither.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.026"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.026", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a027", "note": "The jussive verb takes the supplied “Let” and is headed on “taste”; its explicit compound subject is aligned separately.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.027"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.027", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019", "t027"], "target_head": "t027"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a028", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.028"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.028", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t028"], "target_head": "t028"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a029", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.029"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.029", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t031"], "target_head": "t031"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a030", "note": "The jussive verb licenses “let them feed,” headed on the lexical verb.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.030"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.030", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t029", "t030", "t032"], "target_head": "t032"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a031", "note": "The waw and negative fuse indivisibly into “nor”; the negative is the source and target lexical anchor.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.031", "WLC.JON.3.7.033"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.033", "status": "noncompositional", "target": ["t033"], "target_head": "t033"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a032", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.032"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.032", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t035"], "target_head": "t035"}, {"id": "JON.3.7.a033", "note": "The shared jussive frame and subject are written only with the preceding verb.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.7.034"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.7.034", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t034"], "target_head": "t034"}], "ref": "JON.3.7", "review_notes": ["The ASV margin's “Hebrew said” explains the contextual main-text rendering “published.”"], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JON.3.8.a001", "note": "The waw is rendered by “but.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a002", "note": "The reflexive/passive verbal form licenses the full phrase “let them be covered,” headed on “covered.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003", "t004", "t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a003", "note": "The noun's adverbial function licenses “with.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006", "t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a004", "note": "The ASV writes no definite article before “man.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.004", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a006", "note": "The waw is rendered by the discontinuous correlative pair “both … and”; “both” belongs to the conjunction's English realization, headed on “and.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008", "t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a007", "note": "The ASV writes no definite article before “beast.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.007", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a009", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a010", "note": "The jussive verb licenses “let them cry,” headed on “cry.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013", "t014", "t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a013", "note": "The prepositional expression “with force” is indivisibly rendered by the adverb “mightily,” headed on the lexical noun in the source.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.013", "WLC.JON.3.8.014"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.014", "status": "noncompositional", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a014", "note": "The waw is rendered by “yea.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.015"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a015", "note": "The jussive verb licenses “let them turn,” headed on “turn.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.016"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020", "t021", "t022"], "target_head": "t022"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a016", "note": "The distributive substantive is rendered by “every one,” headed on “one.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.017"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.017", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t023", "t024"], "target_head": "t024"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a017", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.018"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t025"], "target_head": "t025"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a018", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.019"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t028"], "target_head": "t028"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a019", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.020"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t026"], "target_head": "t026"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a020", "note": "The possessive already determines the phrase, so the agreeing article has no English realization.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.021"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.021", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a021", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.022"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.022", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t027"], "target_head": "t027"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a022", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.023"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.023", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t029"], "target_head": "t029"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a023", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.024"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.024", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t030"], "target_head": "t030"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a024", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.025"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.025", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t031"], "target_head": "t031"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a025", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.026"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.026", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t032"], "target_head": "t032"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a026", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.027"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.027", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t033"], "target_head": "t033"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a027", "note": "As the prepositional predicate, it carries the supplied copula “is” together with “in.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.028"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.028", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t034", "t035"], "target_head": "t035"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a028", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.029"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.029", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t037"], "target_head": "t037"}, {"id": "JON.3.8.a029", "note": "The ASV uses singular “his” for the plural Hebrew suffix's collective referent.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.8.030"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.8.030", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t036"], "target_head": "t036"}], "ref": "JON.3.8", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JON.3.9.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a003", "note": "The ASV supplies the subordinator “whether” for a clause having no Hebrew conjunction; rule 55 therefore makes it added.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a005", "note": "The finite verb takes the auxiliary “will” and lexical verb “turn”; the intervening “not” has no corresponding negator in this clause.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a006", "note": "Hebrew has no negator in the clause about God's turning; the sole source לֹא is s015 and realizes the final “not” at t020.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a009", "note": "The article on אֱלֹהִים is not represented in the ASV's bare “God.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.006", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a011", "note": "The verb is rendered by the phrasal verb “turn away,” headed on its lexical verb.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011", "t012"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a013", "note": "The construct חֲרוֹן is rendered attributively by “fierce” rather than by an of-phrase.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a014", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a016", "note": "The ASV renders this waw as the result connective “that,” as permitted by rule 14's open rendering list.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.014"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a017", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.015"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020"], "target_head": "t020"}, {"id": "JON.3.9.a018", "note": "The finite verb takes its English subject pronoun and lexical verb under rule 17.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.9.016"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.9.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018", "t019"], "target_head": "t019"}], "ref": "JON.3.9", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "JON.3.10.a001", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.001"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a002", "note": "The explicit subject God is aligned separately.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.002"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a003", "note": "The ASV writes no article before “God.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.003"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.003", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.004"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a005", "note": "The definite object marker is not separately rendered.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.005"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.005", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.006"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.007"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.008"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a009", "note": "The subject pronoun realizes the verb's person and number.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.009"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a010", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.010"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.011"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012"], "target_head": "t012"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.012"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a013", "note": "The possessive already determines the phrase, so the agreeing article has no English realization.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.013"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.013", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a014", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.014"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a015", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.015"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a016", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.016"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.016", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a017", "note": "The ASV writes no article before the second “God.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.017"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.017", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a018", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.018"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.018", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t014"], "target_head": "t014"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a019", "note": "The governed preposition is rendered by “of.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.019"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.019", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a020", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.020"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.020", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a021", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.021"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.021", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a022", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.022"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.022", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a023", "note": "The subject pronoun realizes the verb's person and number.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.023"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.023", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t020", "t021"], "target_head": "t021"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a024", "note": "The purpose/complement preposition has no written English complementizer.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.024"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.024", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a025", "note": "With no suffixed subject, the infinitive takes the supplied subject pronoun and modal: “he would do.”", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.025"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.025", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t022", "t023", "t024"], "target_head": "t024"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a026", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.026"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.026", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t025"], "target_head": "t025"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a027", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.027"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.027", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t026"], "target_head": "t026"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a028", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.028"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.028", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t027"], "target_head": "t027"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a029", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.029"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.029", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t031"], "target_head": "t031"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a030", "note": "The subject pronoun realizes the verb's person and number.", "source": ["WLC.JON.3.10.030"], "source_head": "WLC.JON.3.10.030", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t028", "t029"], "target_head": "t029"}, {"id": "JON.3.10.a031", "note": "The object pronoun “it” has no source object morpheme and is therefore separate from the verb.", "source": [], "source_head": null, "status": "added", "target": ["t030"], "target_head": "t030"}], "ref"